From: Loong <1031313955@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: airoha: an7583: probe the real DRAM size

Same problem and same fix as 206 does for an7581: dram_init() took the size
straight from the device tree, and fdt_fixup_memory_banks() then pushed that
number into the kernel's dtb, so a board fitted with a larger part than the
dts admits to ran with the excess unreachable.

The two SoCs' init.c are line-for-line identical apart from the name in
print_cpuinfo() and the mem_map variable, and the probe itself is pure
address aliasing -- it writes an anchor low in DRAM, writes again one
candidate size higher, and sees whether the second write wrapped onto the
first.  It touches no SoC register and no controller state, so it carries
over unchanged.

The anchor sits above the ATF reservation at the bottom of DRAM, and both
words are restored before returning, so this runs safely before relocation.

Not verified on hardware: no AN7583 board on hand.  On an7581 the same code
was checked against mmap-aliased memory for the 512 MiB, 1 GiB and 2 GiB
cases; nothing in it is SoC-specific, but a first boot on real hardware
should still confirm the reported size.

--- a/arch/arm/mach-airoha/an7583/init.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-airoha/an7583/init.c
@@ -16,9 +16,57 @@ int print_cpuinfo(void)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The device tree carries a conservative size, because one image ships to
+ * boards fitted with different parts and nothing in the boot chain reports
+ * the real one -- BL2 configures the controller and moves on.  Find it by
+ * address aliasing instead: on a part smaller than the address being probed,
+ * a write high up wraps around and lands back on the low anchor.
+ *
+ * The anchor sits above the ATF reservation at the bottom of DRAM, and both
+ * words are put back before returning, so this is safe to run this early.
+ */
+static ulong an7583_probe_ram_size(ulong base)
+{
+	volatile u32 *lo = (volatile u32 *)(base + SZ_2M);
+	u32 save_lo = *lo;
+	ulong size;
+
+	for (size = SZ_512M; size < SZ_2G; size <<= 1) {
+		volatile u32 *hi = (volatile u32 *)((ulong)lo + size);
+		u32 save_hi = *hi;
+
+		*lo = 0x5a5aa5a5;
+		*hi = 0xa5a55a5a;
+		__asm__ __volatile__("dsb sy" : : : "memory");
+
+		if (*lo != 0x5a5aa5a5) {
+			/* Wrapped, so *hi and *lo are the same word. */
+			*hi = save_hi;
+			*lo = save_lo;
+
+			return size;
+		}
+
+		*hi = save_hi;
+	}
+
+	*lo = save_lo;
+
+	return SZ_2G;
+}
+
 int dram_init(void)
 {
-	return fdtdec_setup_mem_size_base();
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = fdtdec_setup_mem_size_base();
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	gd->ram_size = an7583_probe_ram_size(gd->ram_base);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 int dram_init_banksize(void)
